<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Mihranid Principality of Albania</h1><p class="st-meta">630 CE – 822 CE (approx.) · capital Partav</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of Persian origin that revived local rule in Caucasian Albania and steered it from Sasanian control through the Arab conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihranid-dynasty">Mihranids</a>, a branch of a great Parthian noble family, came to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Caucasian Albania</a> in the late 6th century and held the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gardman">Gardman</a>. Around 630, with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> in crisis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varaz-grigor">Varaz Grigor</a> became ruler of all <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, taking the title of prince and ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Partav</a>, modern Barda.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanshir">Javanshir</a>, the best-known prince, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> and then submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> in 667, while repelling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> raids. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihranid-dynasty">Mihranids</a> patronised the Albanian church and Christian scholarship; the History of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movses-kaghankatvatsi">Movses Kaghankatvatsi</a> praises Javanshir. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Partav</a> grew as a trading city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kura-river">Kura</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanshir">Javanshir</a> was murdered in 680, and the princes became tributaries of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>. The line ended in 822 when the last prince, Varaz-Tiridates II, was killed, and his lands passed to Armenian princely houses such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-khachen">Khachen</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 630 CE – 822 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.24%;width:3.82%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>630 CE – 822 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Partav</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Varaz Grigor, Javanshir, Varaz-Tiridates I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Caucasian Albanian; Armenian; Middle Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mihranids, Principality of Caucasian Albania, Arranshahs</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=726&amp;focus=mihranid-principality-of-albania" aria-label="Mihranid Principality of Albania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5835 737 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mihranid Principality of Albania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6152 991h0M6357 1235h0M6134 1224h0M6134 1